## T0604 -- `+` between a decimal and an int: `+` never converts its operands.
## command: lume build   (this file shows the diagnostic: the gate runs a copy named .src; T0604_plus_never_converts.fixed.src is the corrected program)
## fix: use operands of one type (here the int 1); for text, str(n) converts a number
fn f(a: int) -> int = 1.0 + a
print f(2)
